abstract: >-
  R(B_66, B_67) = 267, the case n = 67 of Wesley's conjecture R(B_{n-1}, B_n) = 4n - 1, which no
  earlier construction covered. The extremal graph is a two-block circulant graph over Z_133 whose
  connection sets are unions of orbits of the cube roots of unity modulo 133. The repository holds
  the paper, a Lean 4 kernel check of the graph (standard axioms only), independent checks in C and
  Python, the search, and a dated priority check.
